From e8835220fdcc7df876134404db1a67d4c49c0463 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anthoine Bourgeois <anthoine.bourgeois@vates.tech>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 15:28:16 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] qcow2: fix use-after-free of s->bh when a commit races driver
 close

s->lock only protected the insertion into s->inflight, not the
qemu_bh_schedule(s->bh) that immediately followed it. Nothing stopped
_qcow2_close() from running concurrently on another thread and freeing
s->bh (the worker thread's teardown deletes it, and the memory is actually
released later by an aio_bh_poll() inside blk_unref()) while a
commit-family caller was still reading it.

Signed-off-by: Anthoine Bourgeois <anthoine.bourgeois@vates.tech>
---
 drivers/block-qcow2.c | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/block-qcow2.c b/drivers/block-qcow2.c
index 6b5a3da4..18592247 100644
--- a/drivers/block-qcow2.c
+++ b/drivers/block-qcow2.c
@@ -596,11 +596,15 @@ _qcow2_close(td_driver_t *driver)
 
 	DBG(TLOG_WARN, "qcow2_close\n");
 
+        /*
+         * Kick while still holding the lock: the thread only checks
+         * driver_opened after taking s->lock, so kicking after unlock
+         * risks the bh/AioContext already being torn down.
+         */
 	pthread_mutex_lock(&s->lock);
 	s->driver_opened = false;
-	pthread_mutex_unlock(&s->lock);
-
 	qemu_bh_schedule(s->bh);
+	pthread_mutex_unlock(&s->lock);
 
 	// Ignore return, qcow2_open() always return NULL; or will abort
 	qemu_thread_join(&s->thread);
